  "changes": [
    "Workspace footer actions now acquire Rust graph-owned controls: kind 3 is an opaque workspace ID and kind 4 is fixed footer chrome (pin/settings). Separate namespaces cannot alias pin or workspace domain IDs.",
    "Reconcile the complete footer snapshot before native button replacement. Emoji/name/profile/catalogue rebuilds preserve logical IDs; old adapters lose their lease, removed workspaces retire and reinsertions allocate fresh IDs. Pin/settings are not rebound by workspace-dot refresh. Detaching the shell drops the scope and invalidates any retained handles.",
    "Three new pure Rust tests cover footer namespaces, reorder/replacement/retirement/reinsertion and transactional invalid snapshots. A compiled-only browser case retains an old workspace adapter, changes its emoji, checks logical identity and stale AX rejection, then changes selection and clears the emoji."
  ],
